# project: kitchen-renovation
VAR council_bounces = 0

=== gather_quotes ===
Collect renovation quotes from two contractors for the kitchen.
Done when both written quotes are in hand and comparable.
* [Both quotes in hand] -> choose_contractor

=== choose_contractor ===
We and Sam compare the two quotes and pick a contractor. Sam has equal say.
+ [Contractor chosen together] @human -> budget_signoff

=== budget_signoff ===
Sam reviews and signs off on the budget before any deposit is paid.
+ [Sam approves budget, pay deposit] @human -> permit_application
+ [Budget not approved, revisit choice] @human ~loop~ -> choose_contractor

=== permit_application ===
Submit the permit application to the council and await their response.
+ [Permit granted] -> demolition_build
+ {council_bounces < 2} [Council bounced it with questions] -> address_council_questions
+ {council_bounces >= 2} [Bounced again, time to rethink] @human -> rethink_design

=== address_council_questions ===
Answer the council's questions and resubmit the application.
~ council_bounces += 1
+ [Resubmitted] ~loop~ -> permit_application

=== rethink_design ===
Rework the kitchen design with the contractor to address the council's objections.
+ [Revised design ready, resubmit] @human ~loop~ -> permit_application

=== demolition_build ===
Contractor demolishes the old kitchen and builds the new one to the permitted design.
* [Build complete] -> snag_walkthrough

=== snag_walkthrough ===
Walk through the kitchen with the contractor and list snags to fix.
Repeat walkthroughs until we are happy with the result.
+ [Snags found, contractor fixes them] ~loop~ -> snag_walkthrough
+ [We're happy with the kitchen] @human -> final_signoff

=== final_signoff ===
Sam and I both inspect the finished kitchen; final payment is released only
after both of us sign off.
+ [Both sign off, release final payment] @human -> END
+ [Not satisfied, more snags] @human ~loop~ -> snag_walkthrough
